    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current Pollution Under Control (PUC) Certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A valid PUC, issued within the last 30 days, confirms that your car meets the latest emission standards and is road‑worthy.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Your vehicle’s motor insurance policy should be active and the policy number clearly printed on the certificate. This covers any accidental damage during normal use.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The Inter‑State Transport Authority (IBA) requires a consignment bilty that lists the vehicle details, route, and carrier information. The bilty must be signed by the consignor and carrier.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>All these documents should be scanned and submitted to your carrier at least 48 hours before the scheduled pickup. The carrier will verify each item and keep a copy in the transport manifest to avoid any disputes at the destination.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">While the above documents handle legal and regulatory compliance, the <strong>100 % declared‑value marine transit insurance</strong> is what gives you peace of mind during the actual transit.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This coverage ensures that if your vehicle is damaged, stolen, or otherwise compromised while on the road, the carrier will reimburse you for the full declared value of the car – no deduction for depreciation or incidental losses.</span></li></ul>
<p>The insurance is typically included in the freight cost, but you should request a copy of the policy and confirm the coverage limits and exclusions before signing the final contract.</p>

<p>In summary, always have the self‑attested RC, current PUC, valid insurance, and IBA‑approved consignment bilty ready. Pair these with a comprehensive 100 % declared‑value marine transit insurance, and you’ll be fully protected from start to finish.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


